1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,844
Ravi is opening a second
Chai Corner next month.

2
00:00:04,143 --> 00:00:05,515
But he has no plan.

3
00:00:05,515 --> 00:00:07,251
Just one wish: sell more.

4
00:00:07,801 --> 00:00:10,817
On day one, the milk
runs out by ten o'clock.

5
00:00:11,117 --> 00:00:13,475
Nobody knows who should open the shop.

6
00:00:13,775 --> 00:00:16,315
And at night, nobody
knows if sales went up.

7
00:00:16,965 --> 00:00:18,624
Wishing is not enough.

8
00:00:18,624 --> 00:00:20,074
Ravi needs a plan.

9
00:00:20,774 --> 00:00:22,049
So, what is planning?

10
00:00:22,349 --> 00:00:26,197
Planning means deciding in advance
what to do, how, when, and who will

11
00:00:26,197 --> 00:00:27,097
do it.

12
00:00:27,354 --> 00:00:28,318
Ravi decides.

13
00:00:28,318 --> 00:00:33,081
Serve chai at the new outlet, same
recipe, from seven, and Meena runs it.

14
00:00:33,731 --> 00:00:35,525
Planning follows seven steps.

15
00:00:35,975 --> 00:00:36,875
One.

16
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:39,096
Set objectives: what you want to achieve.

17
00:00:39,446 --> 00:00:40,346
Two.

18
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:41,222
Develop premises.

19
00:00:41,222 --> 00:00:45,124
These are forecasts, like how
many people will walk past.

20
00:00:45,474 --> 00:00:46,374
Three.

21
00:00:46,061 --> 00:00:50,298
Identify alternatives: the college,
the bus stand, or the market.

22
00:00:50,648 --> 00:00:51,548
Four.

23
00:00:51,192 --> 00:00:54,575
Evaluate them: rent, crowd,
and other tea stalls.

24
00:00:54,925 --> 00:00:55,825
Five.

25
00:00:55,523 --> 00:00:56,836
Choose the best.

26
00:00:56,836 --> 00:00:58,374
The bus stand wins.

27
00:00:58,724 --> 00:00:59,624
Six.

28
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:03,420
Make supporting plans, like hiring
two helpers and ordering milk.

29
00:01:03,770 --> 00:01:04,670
And seven.

30
00:01:04,590 --> 00:01:06,184
Implement and follow up.

31
00:01:06,184 --> 00:01:09,486
Open the shop, then check
every week that it works.

32
00:01:10,136 --> 00:01:12,438
Plans also come in three sizes.

33
00:01:12,788 --> 00:01:17,685
Strategic plans are the big picture,
for years, like five outlets in five

34
00:01:17,685 --> 00:01:18,585
years.

35
00:01:18,673 --> 00:01:23,379
Tactical plans break that into this
year's steps, like opening outlet two.

36
00:01:23,729 --> 00:01:28,361
And operational plans are the daily
details, like tomorrow's shift chart.

37
00:01:29,011 --> 00:01:32,228
But Ravi's wish, sell more,
is too vague to be a goal.

38
00:01:32,578 --> 00:01:37,664
In 1981, George Doran wrote in
Management Review that good goals should

39
00:01:37,664 --> 00:01:38,608
be SMART.

40
00:01:38,958 --> 00:01:40,954
Today, the letters mean this.

41
00:01:40,954 --> 00:01:41,854
Specific.

42
00:01:41,676 --> 00:01:43,928
Cups of chai, at the new outlet.

43
00:01:44,278 --> 00:01:45,178
Measurable.

44
00:01:45,119 --> 00:01:48,141
Five hundred a day, so
Kabir can count them.

45
00:01:48,491 --> 00:01:49,391
Achievable.

46
00:01:49,354 --> 00:01:51,984
The busy bus stand makes that possible.

47
00:01:52,334 --> 00:01:53,234
Relevant.

48
00:01:53,045 --> 00:01:54,877
It pays for the new outlet.

49
00:01:55,227 --> 00:01:56,486
And time-bound.

50
00:01:56,486 --> 00:01:57,451
By March.

51
00:01:57,801 --> 00:02:02,403
So, sell more becomes: sell five
hundred cups a day at the new outlet by

52
00:02:02,403 --> 00:02:03,303
March.

53
00:02:03,644 --> 00:02:04,573
Quick check.

54
00:02:04,573 --> 00:02:07,540
Asha's goal is to make
two hundred cups a day.

55
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:09,503
Which SMART letter is missing?

56
00:02:11,403 --> 00:02:12,303
Time-bound!

57
00:02:12,271 --> 00:02:13,813
It has no deadline.

58
00:02:13,813 --> 00:02:15,796
Add one, like by Friday.

59
00:02:16,396 --> 00:02:17,408
So, remember.

60
00:02:17,708 --> 00:02:21,297
Planning means deciding in
advance what, how, when, and who.

61
00:02:21,647 --> 00:02:26,098
It moves step by step: objectives,
premises, alternatives, choice, and

62
00:02:26,098 --> 00:02:26,998
follow up.

63
00:02:27,281 --> 00:02:31,937
And good goals are SMART: specific,
measurable, achievable, relevant, and

64
00:02:31,937 --> 00:02:32,837
time-bound.

65
00:02:33,323 --> 00:02:37,445
Next time, Ravi organizes his
growing team into departments.
